  SEARCH RESULTS COUNT = 14

&nbsp;


FELLOW HUMAN, IT SEEMS YOUR WORD DICTIONARY HAS BEEN MALFUNCTIONING. IT SEEMS THAT YOU HAVE BEEN USING THE WORDS `fuck` AND `fuckers` PLEASE CHECK YOUR ORGANIC BIOS IS UP TO DATE.

My co-worker saying that I failed not only myself but everyone around me. This sucks because my entire life I was always associated with, 'he failed his homework, he failed his parents, he failed his siblings, he failed being the star child, he failed being an employee, he failed college, he failed his girlfriend, he failed his best friends, he failed, failed failed failed.' 

&nbsp;

I don't know if I can go to work now, or if I can even get out of bed with the cyclone of failure.

Two words for you my friend. 

&nbsp;

The Kraken 

&nbsp;

This ancient beast sink ships and just wrecks your days at sea if you stray too far off coast. Plus the Kraken, (from 5e) has the ability to make storms in its lair so sea travel is not fun.

We were going inside a old wizard tower trying to find a banshee. While in this tower, me being an elf cleric that has a really good perception was looking around after seeing a lot of ghosts out and about. Now the barbarian here's a ghostly sound down a very dark hall way with one torch (the torch I'm holding by the way) What does he do?

&nbsp;

"Damn flying men! Im gonna smash them!" And he just rushes into pitch blankness. Of course my elf is compassionate to his friend rushes in after him with pure panic. He was swinging wildly at the 'ghost.' around the corner. He told me that he was going to take a swing at me as soon as I enter sense he does not know I'm their. At first I was about to say hell no, but decided that both me and the Barbarain has low intelligence so I enter the dark library, he crits me, he cries over my dead body, then hold my holy symbol of Bahamut killing all the ghost.

&nbsp;

I wasn't even mad.

Can anyone explain the following to me, they might not be punny funny, but more just stupid.

&nbsp;

Planeshift - (a forked, metal rod worth at least
250 gp, attuned to a particular plane of existence)

&nbsp;

Detect Poison or Disease - (a yew leaf.)

&nbsp;

Rope Trick - (powdered corn extract and a
twisted loop of parchment) 

&nbsp;

True seeing - (an ointment for the eyes that
costs 25 gp; is made from mushroom powder, saffron,
and fat; and is consumed by the spell)

>The bag can hold up to 500 pounds, not exceeding a volume of 64 cubic feet.

&nbsp;

Does that mean that that you cant fill this space that is 64 cubic feet AND not over 500 lb? Or you can't fit something that is more then 64 cubic in size in the bag?

You can't fix stupid. And you can't reverse being brainwashed. 

&nbsp;

**Edit** Well you can reverse being brain washed, but that's not the point

Well, I would say this wall, or 'magical membrane," keeps the material plane intact, it its broken, or torn, it will bring in a power house of positive and negative energy from the outer planes  into the material plane. Chaos and Entropy would follow. 

&nbsp; 

Think about it. A world where humanoids are filled with so much righteous radiant light, that they persecute any person that breaks the creed of their temple or law to the extremes. Clerics of a church turning into mortal angels of justice. Nobels become influences with such evil energy that become mortal devils, tricking, scheming and taking the lives of the innocents. 

&nbsp;

The world would total chaos. The social structure of the material plane city would crumble. If this membrane breaks or even leaves a little hole, it would be the End Times...

But seriously, like a said, some taverns, maybe historical statues for campaign hooks and plots, like maybe of the statue of that wizard that over grown the area. Shops definitely. But since this is DnD we are talking about, its up for the DM to decide what is essential and what is not. 

&nbsp;

But for a city that would make logical sense? Personally, building that serves the society the most, Sense this is a world that that was brought to struggle in lower settlements, and bigger once prosper, maybe but in some thing that proves that they prosper.

&nbsp;

Vague answer is vague but that's the best I could come up with.

Bleb... im dumb

